# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
# macOS writes a custom folder icon into a file named `Icon` followed by
# a carriage return, and `Icon?` is the usual way to catch it. But `?` is
# a wildcard: it also matched `icons`, which silently excluded
# assets/icons - sixty-four SVGs the interface cannot start without. A
# clean clone built and came up with no icons at all, and nothing said
# why.
#
# The rule stays and the directory it should never have touched is named,
# because a rule written as an actual carriage return does not survive a
# line-ending normalisation.
Icon?
!assets/icons/
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

